# Example 36: Population-level calibration (NEW)
# Recovers the three free dFBA colony parameters (maximum O2 uptake,
# energy scale, division threshold) from colony-level mixed observables
# only -- no per-cell state is read (doc/18-programmable-cell-population-simulation.md §13 Design 4).
#
# The probe is a short co-located shared-batch colony that divides one to
# two times in-window.  The fit runs three nearly independent stages:
#   1. metabolic probe (growth rate + core/edge O2/acetate) -> oxygen
#   2. division-free energy probe (mean cell energy grows linearly with
#      the per-tick accumulation rate) -> energy scale
#   3. division probe (time-averaged mean/total/newborn energy + colony
#      size) -> division threshold, with the other two held fixed
# The division block alone cannot separate scale from threshold (both its
# mean and newborn energies scale like threshold - c*scale); reading the
# scale division-free is what makes the two knobs separable.
#
# Runtime ~1-2 min (the fit budget is dominated by the division probe).

#sim kind=population_calibration
#sim n_samples=12 refine_rounds=2 division_ticks=12 fit_seed=0
#sim output=best,passed

#config backend=fba
